    "function": "Catalyzes the cleavage of sphingomyelin, a major lipid in eukaryotic cells, into ceramide and phosphocholine, which are then utilized by M.tuberculosis as carbon, nitrogen and phosphorus sources, respectively. Thus, enables M.tuberculosis to utilize sphingomyelin as a source of several essential nutrients for intracellular growth during infection. Furthermore, lyses erythrocytes and constitutes the main hemolytic factor of M.tuberculosis",
